======================================================================
THE MULTIPLE COMPARISONS PROBLEM
======================================================================
Total comparisons made: 21 (t-tests) + 21 (Fisher's exact) = 42
At alpha=0.05, we expect ~2.10 false positives by chance alone, even if none of the true underlying differences existed.
Some of the 'significant' results found in Steps 4-5 are therefore likely to be noise, not real differences — correction is needed before acting on them.

